92186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1031 "Systems of Equations as Augmented Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1033 148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1034 0.6027738609637455 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050765 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "64dbabd7-08e6-5435-b006-ab4997312f47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428346 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428347 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428348 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428349 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428350 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1031 "LU Factorization of 3x3 Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1033 1780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051083 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7fcb6c0b-c77e-5abe-8b04-125d08ffe36e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119610 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119610 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](images/f1/f1124e83e3b7614557a1a6de54523cc99f62ba2a52af1da8e4d22e14466ce020.svg)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119610 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9552ad30-9d46-5884-9877-18ca8842c252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119610 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/a1/a185a6fd91c78ed3e291b3ac8b99f9430290e5d8c1060a7d97317efc230aeb40.svg)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/1e/1e780d384ca1fd957d742bbd047399c558ab016d187ce4cf71682546673aba35.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](images/58/58da62903247cf6dfdf33be86293c181ef5184048ca7cd6c921360e5d202f353.svg)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/e0/e0563dde4944ecbe2ccb98bc91246fa18c7a808df96ab77f9f8efb5510084677.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](images/a8/a84088cff2a3589652ef7cabf09e3d8429fad7797ea20d44a416f85dcc7f9b65.svg)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119611 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4777" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119611 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](images/a1/a13a7752a224bdabc27558a6a41e2b24d3c7918af1ca4d9cff802dcb54259238.svg)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119611 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "24bc4954-462b-5066-83d4-8a4a87efc7b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119611 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/60/605f569e0b4a54d2ca68d7b3330a2a0ebb06dcaba2b7efa911f58dbffd796fb0.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](images/d2/d259a6740aa32e0e577756375fd85589b815232314511c74dc434a88d0146a3b.svg)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/c5/c5198aa83d3976d992b200f63941261f952282fedb241db780c20c12c97e3ba9.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119706 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8926" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119706 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](images/9d/9d0b186213211813b290f502888f68e0603bc9f77bcd7ea9d6262cb7449c00e7.svg)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119706 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cbefba9a-eda2-5a8e-8bb5-59ea4175b835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119706 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/42/4298fe244fd6c66c7623ad508c97b96464321387506aa1e4be5e2399a5c9a862.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 66\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=66.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](images/a8/a86dfd0e07b8c415e526764cf9f7ba8f020609bf7b13cc90536deba868ec4aa6.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186377114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186390757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186558571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119799 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119800 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759