x},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3a99bb0-e72d-5183-bc18-0817eb820005" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241124 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-36.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241144 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241144 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105930" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241144 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241144 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241144 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f817b0d9-deca-51e1-aedb-860b4e44d9bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241144 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=-2 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2-9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2-9(-2) \\\\  & =16, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1+4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1+4(-2)-(16) \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241145 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241145 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241145 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241145 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186241145 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90586eea-75b4-50dc-8971-26e34a9a2816" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241145 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end